    "blocks": [
      {
        "id": "p1",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Three years ago, I started working at the University of Leeds. Having moved to a new city, I was looking for activities that would help me make some new friends. I noticed that a community school was offering Chinese evening classes. Without much thought, I signed up for a beginner class."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p2",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "I had no plans to move to China. I just wanted to learn a new language. It was not something I had "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "previously",
            "ref": "v-previously"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " done. I was raised to speak fluent English and Spanish. But I think there should be a huge difference between learning a language as a child and as an adult."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p3",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "There was one lesson a week, each lasting 90 minutes. Mr. Kong, the teacher, was "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "energetic",
            "ref": "v-energetic"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": ". For each class, he would teach us what seemed like hundreds of new words. "
          },
          {
            "t": "underline",
            "v": "After each lesson, I felt as if my brain had been placed in a deep-fat fryer"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": ". Fortunately, after a few months, I got used to this. I began to realise that the more my brain ached after class, the more information I had taken in. Between weekly classes, my mind would reorder and make sense of the "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "chaos",
            "ref": "v-chaos"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p4",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "The University of Leeds had more than 6,000 international students. Finding Chinese students who would like to practise English in exchange for Chinese was not difficult. My new Chinese friends helped me go over everything I had learnt in class."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p5",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "I think Chinese grammar is easier than English or Spanish grammar. But there are so many words and "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "idioms",
            "zh": "习语"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "! Nevertheless, I am ready to "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "overcome",
            "ref": "v-overcome"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " any difficulty and become fluent in Chinese."
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
